# tools/rye_bridge_cycle_witness.rish -- the compiler that builds everything, given a guard of its own.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. Rye builds every `.rye` file in this tree -- Caravan's hundred and ten rungs, the
# crypto ladder, Aurora's freestanding seed, and Rye itself. It is the most Lindy-exposed tool the
# tree owns, and until this witness it carried no check on its own build bridge at all. A fault
# there is a fault under everything.
#
# WHAT WENT WRONG. `bridge_rye_tree` walks a root `.rye` file and every `.rye` it imports,
# recursively, staging each as a `.zig` the toolchain can read. Its visited set was appended AFTER
# the walk into a file's own imports rather than before -- so while a cycle was being traversed
# nothing was ever marked seen, and two files importing each other recursed until the stack died.
# Not a named error, not a diagnostic: a segfault (REDS %125). Beneath it sat a second fault of the
# same family -- the file the walk STARTS from bridged to `foo.rye.zig` while every dependency
# bridged to `foo.zig`, so a module that imported the root by name asked the toolchain for a file
# the bridge had never written. One file had two names, and only the cycle ever asked.
#
# HOW IT WAS FOUND. By measurement rather than by reading. A carry fold on the Caravan ladder wanted
# four base modules to import the shared harness that already imports them, so the question "does
# Rye allow a mutual import?" was asked of the compiler rather than of memory. It answered with a
# segmentation fault.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal, over `tools/fixtures/rye_bridge_cycle_control.sh`.
#   Two `.rye` files that import each other bridge, compile, link, and run, with a value crossing
#   the cycle and returning unchanged.
#   The root of the walk is reachable BY NAME from one of its own dependencies -- one file, one
#   bridged name.
#   An import chain deeper than `max_bridge_depth` refuses by NAME rather than exhausting the
#   stack, and the bound is read off the source rather than recited here, since a number written
#   into a comment drifts the moment the source moves (REDS %110).
#   Every staged `.zig` is swept afterward, so a bridge run leaves its corpus as it found it.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That mutual imports are good design -- they are merely legal now, as they
# already are in Zig's own file-as-struct model. Single-strandedness still argues for a graph a
# reader can hold, and this witness guards the compiler rather than the taste.
#
# The corpus is written for the question and thrown away after. The tree holds no mutual `.rye`
# import today, so a scan of the tree would have proved the bridge correct by proving nothing
# reached the fault -- which is REDS %102's family exactly.
#
# No network, no key, no funds, no device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/rye_bridge_cycle_witness.rish

say "rye-bridge-cycle: Language EN -- Rye builds every .rye file this tree holds, and until now it carried no guard on its own build bridge."
say "rye-bridge-cycle: Style Radiant -- the fault was measured rather than reasoned about; the compiler was asked a question and answered with a segfault, so the question became a witness."
say "rye-bridge-cycle: Lens TAME -- safety first: no unbounded recursion, a named error at a named bound, and both the welcome and the refusal proven on a corpus whose answer is known by construction."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/rye_bridge_cycle_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "rye-bridge-cycle: the build bridge did not survive its own corpus -- ${control.err}"
say control.out

assert control.out contains "verdict=ok" else "rye-bridge-cycle: the control must balance before it is believed"
assert control.out contains "CYCLE_BUILD ok" else "rye-bridge-cycle: two files importing each other must bridge and compile"
assert control.out contains "root_reached_from_dependency=yes" else "rye-bridge-cycle: the root of the walk must be reachable by name from its own dependency -- one file, one bridged name"
assert control.out contains "CYCLE_RUN ok" else "rye-bridge-cycle: the built cycle must run, with the value crossing it unchanged"
assert control.out contains "STAGED_LEFTOVERS count=0" else "rye-bridge-cycle: every staged .zig must be swept away after a bridge run"
assert control.out contains "DEEP_REFUSAL named" else "rye-bridge-cycle: a chain past the bound must refuse BY NAME rather than exhaust the stack"

say "GREEN: rye-bridge-cycle -- the build bridge terminates on a cyclic import graph, names its bound when a chain runs past it, reaches its own root by one name, and leaves no staging behind."
